Building argus-scanner
======================

The source package contains the argus Python sources and debian/ only; there
are no vendored wheels and no third-party binaries, so no version of
debian/source/include-binaries is needed and the orig tarball stays small.

Build dependencies
------------------
  debhelper-compat (= 13), python3, python3-pip, python3-setuptools,
  python3-wheel

The build is offline: debian/rules calls

  python3 -m pip wheel --no-deps --no-build-isolation .

and installs the resulting pure-Python wheel into

  /usr/lib/argus-scanner/argus_scanner-<version>-py3-none-any.whl

If the wheel turns out not to be architecture independent, the build fails.

  dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b

Runtime provisioning
--------------------
The Python runtime is not built here.  debian/postinst runs
argus-setup-runtime, which creates a virtual environment in
/var/lib/argus-scanner/runtime and installs the wheel plus its dependencies
(including Semgrep) from the package index.  That keeps the binary package
small and independent of the local ABI, at the cost of requiring network
access during installation.  Offline installations use
`argus-setup-runtime --wheelhouse DIR` or set ARGUS_WHEELHOUSE.

What the package installs
-------------------------
  /usr/lib/argus-scanner/argus_scanner-<version>-py3-none-any.whl
  /usr/bin/argus
  /usr/bin/argus-gui
  /usr/bin/argus-setup-runtime
  man pages and /usr/share/doc/argus-scanner/

Rebuilding for another platform is not necessary: the wheel is pure Python
and the dependencies are resolved on the target machine.

 -- Ivan Moshkin <ilevanov1900@gmail.com>
